      "html": "<span class=\"ds-local\">ON THIS DEVICE</span>",
      "css": ".ds-local{display:inline-flex;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 10px;background:#E8F1E9;color:#11634E;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:11px;line-height:16px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Financial card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "financial-card",
      "description": "Default borderless FinancialCard, illustrated with the first-use account prompt. It adds no ledger records.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-financial-card\"><h2 class=\"ds-card-title\">Let’s start with your balance.</h2><p class=\"ds-card-copy\">Add your first account and its opening balance. Your ledger starts empty and stays on this device.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-financial-card{padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:#FFFFFF;color:#182D35;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-card-title{margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:26px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.3px}.ds-card-copy{margin:8px 0 0;color:#586B70;font-size:15px;line-height:23px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Balance card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "balance-card",
      "description": "Fresh-ledger BalanceCard: zero recorded balance, zero accounts and no period totals until an account exists. Source props later supply real balance and monthly income/expenses; this specimen has no visibility runtime.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-balance\"><div class=\"ds-balance-top\"><div><p class=\"ds-balance-label\">Recorded balance</p><p class=\"ds-balance-caption\">0 local accounts</p></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-eye\" aria-label=\"Hide balance\" aria-expanded=\"true\"><svg width=\"23\" height=\"23\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2 12s3.5-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.5 7-10 7S2 12 2 12Z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"/></svg></button></div><p class=\"ds-balance-amount\">RM0.00</p><p class=\"ds-balance-caption\">Based on the records you add.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-balance{padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:#11634E;color:#FFFFFF;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-balance-top{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px}.ds-balance-label{margin:0;color:#E0F0E6;font-size:15px;line-height:23px}.ds-balance-caption{margin:0;color:#E0F0E6;font-size:12px;line-height:18px}.ds-eye{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-end;min-width:48px;min-height:48px;padding:0;border:0;background:transparent;color:#E0F0E6;cursor:pointer}.ds-eye:hover{cursor:pointer}.ds-eye:active{opacity:.6}.ds-eye:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #D8EFCC;outline-offset:3px}.ds-balance-amount{margin:12px 0 4px;font-size:40px;line-height:52px;letter-spacing:-1.2px;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Transaction row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Editable TransactionItem expense with category tile, explicit direction and trailing tabular amount. Illustrative specimen content is not seeded into the real ledger; no editor runtime is included.",
      "html": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-transaction\" aria-label=\"Nasi Kandar Pelita, expense, money out, RM12.50, Food and drinks, Touch 'n Go\"><span class=\"ds-category\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 3v6m3-6v6m3-6v6M4 7h6M7 9v12M17 3c-3 4-4 8 0 9v9m0-18v9\"/></svg></span><div class=\"ds-transaction-detail\"><p class=\"ds-merchant\">Nasi Kandar Pelita</p><p class=\"ds-account\">Food &amp; drinks · Touch ’n Go</p></div><span class=\"ds-transaction-amount\">−RM12.50</span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-transaction{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:48px;width:100%;border:0;background:transparent;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;padding:16px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #E4EAE5;color:#182D35;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-category{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-shrink:0;width:46px;height:46px;border-radius:12px;background:#F9EDE4;color:#A6532D}.ds-transaction-detail{flex:1;min-width:105px}.ds-merchant{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:600}.ds-account{margin:3px 0 0;color:#586B70;font-size:12px;line-height:18px}.ds-transaction-amount{margin-left:auto;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-transaction:hover{cursor:pointer}.ds-transaction:active{opacity:.7}.ds-transaction:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #11634E;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ledger form fields and choices",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "form-field",
      "description": "Persistent labels, plain decimal entry, hint/error feedback and wrapping radio choices from Field/ChoiceGroup. Static specimen states do not implement validation or selection.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-form\"><label class=\"ds-field\"><span class=\"ds-form-label\">Amount (RM)</span><input class=\"ds-field-input\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"12.50\" aria-describedby=\"ds-amount-hint\"><span id=\"ds-amount-hint\" class=\"ds-form-hint\">Use 12.50. Enter a positive amount for every transaction type.</span></label><div class=\"ds-field\"><span id=\"ds-type-label\" class=\"ds-form-label\">Transaction type</span><div role=\"radiogroup\" aria-labelledby=\"ds-type-label\" class=\"ds-choices\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"true\" class=\"ds-choice ds-choice-selected\">Expense</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"false\" class=\"ds-choice\">Income</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"false\" class=\"ds-choice\">Refund</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"false\" class=\"ds-choice\">Transfer</button></div></div><label class=\"ds-field\"><span class=\"ds-form-label\">Opening balance (RM)</span><input class=\"ds-field-input ds-field-invalid\" value=\"12,50\" aria-invalid=\"true\" aria-describedby=\"ds-opening-error\"><span id=\"ds-opening-error\" class=\"ds-form-error\">Enter an amount such as 12.50, with at most two decimal places and no commas.</span></label></div>",
      "css": ".ds-form{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px;color:#182D35;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-field{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}.ds-form-label{font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:600}.ds-field-input{min-width:0;min-height:52px;padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid #74867B;border-radius:12px;background:#FFFFFF;color:#182D35;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:16px}.ds-field-input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #11634E;outline-offset:3px}.ds-field-invalid{border-color:#A6532D}.ds-form-hint,.ds-form-error{font-size:12px;line-height:18px;color:#586B70}.ds-form-error{color:#A6532D}.ds-choices{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}.ds-choice{min-height:48px;padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #E4EAE5;border-radius:12px;background:#FFFFFF;color:#586B70;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}.ds-choice-selected{border-color:#11634E;background:#E8F1E9;color:#11634E}.ds-choice:hover{cursor:pointer}.ds-choice:active{opacity:.7}.ds-choice:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #11634E;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Deletion confirmation",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "confirm-delete",
      "description": "ConfirmDelete surface and navy scrim with explicit consequence and destructive/keep actions. This static illustration does not open a modal, delete data or manage focus.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-scrim\"><section class=\"ds-delete-dialog\" aria-label=\"Deletion confirmation specimen\"><h2 class=\"ds-delete-title\">Delete this transaction?</h2><p class=\"ds-delete-copy\">It will be removed and affected account balances will be recalculated. This cannot be undone.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-delete-confirm\">Confirm deletion</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-delete-keep\">Keep it</button></section></div>",
      "css": ".ds-scrim{display:flex;justify-content:center;padding:24px;background:rgba(24,45,53,.55)}.ds-delete-dialog{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;width:100%;max-width:440px;padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:#F7F8F4;color:#182D35;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-delete-title{margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:26px;letter-spacing:-.3px;font-weight:700}.ds-delete-copy{margin:0;color:#586B70;font-size:15px;line-height:23px}.ds-delete-confirm,.ds-delete-keep{min-height:48px;padding:12px 16px;border:0;border-radius:12px;background:#A6532D;color:#FFFFFF;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:600;white-space:normal;cursor:pointer}.ds-delete-keep{background:#E8F1E9;color:#11634E}.ds-delete-confirm:hover,.ds-delete-keep:hover{cursor:pointer}.ds-delete-confirm:active,.ds-delete-keep:active{opacity:.72}.ds-delete-confirm:focus-visible,.ds-delete-keep:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #11634E;outline-offset:3px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Daily Planner",
    "overview": "BakiBuddy makes everyday money feel understandable through a calm reading order, recognizable category symbols, and clear amounts. Phase 2 extends the established premium, clean, friendly, and trustworthy system: deep navy text, a strong emerald balance surface, warm off-white pages, and softly rounded cards.\n\nThis records the implemented React Native + Expo system for Android and iOS, with a supplemental React Native Web preview. It is a light-only system. The local SQLite ledger starts empty and presents only accounts and records the user adds; unavailable actions name their future phase. Historical fictional fixtures remain outside the real ledger. No raster composition was approved or generated; the implementation and its production browser captures are the visual evidence.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Emerald carries financial emphasis and selected states.",
      "Manrope headings and tabular money sit beside familiar platform body text.",
      "A single scrolling column, tonal surfaces, and chronological rows keep density practical.",
      "Native navigation, scalable text, and visible local-storage context support trust."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning Before Color Rule",
        "body": "Income/refunds carry a plus sign, expenses a minus sign, and transfers explicit transfer copy. Color reinforces those meanings; it never supplies the only distinction.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Amount Rule",
        "body": "Preserve the display money face, tabular numerals, explicit MYR formatting, and room for values. Editable amounts remain plain decimal text under an RM field label. Do not replace readable amounts with decorative counters.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tonal Surface Rule",
        "body": "Use the established surface colors and spacing to define hierarchy. The implemented cards do not need a new shadow vocabulary.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use semantic tokens and the existing components before introducing a new visual primitive.",
      "Do keep local-storage disclosure visible and distinguish recorded balances, period totals and unavailable forecasts.",
      "Do preserve tabular MYR amounts, explicit transaction direction, and neutral transfer treatment.",
      "Do retain native navigation, safe-area support, default text scaling, and at least 48-unit control targets.",
      "Do allow headers, amounts, and chronological rows to wrap on compact screens.",
      "Do keep future actions disabled or explicitly unavailable with a phase label.",
      "Do use persistent field labels, specific hints, visible selected states and recoverable validation feedback."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add dark-mode claims, animated money counters, or an unimplemented motion scale.",
      "Don't use category color as the only way to explain transaction kind or budget status.",
      "Don't promote component-local colors or the unused emeraldDark token into new global roles without a deliberate implementation change.",
      "Don't seed fictional fixtures into the real ledger or present them beside real totals.",
      "Don't treat browser captures or native bundle generation as successful Android/iOS runtime testing.",
      "Don't add budget forecasts, charts, imports, OCR, AI, or other later-phase behavior under this documentation pass."
    ]
  }
}
